-- S23 Maharashtra prose — siddhatek
-- Verdict matrix: 7 go / 3 skip / 2 wait
-- Anchors: Siddhivinayak — 3rd Ashtavinayak in yatra order, ONLY right-trunk Ganesh murti (siddhi direction — opposite to standard left-trunk), Bhima river island in Karjat tehsil Ahmednagar district, 1810 reconstruction by Punyashlok Ahilyabai Holkar, saint Vishnu sought blessings here before Madhu-Kaitabh battle, 100km Pune via Daund. Override: Jul/Aug=SKIP not wait (Bhima river floods, island boat access suspends)

INSERT INTO destination_months (
  destination_id, month, verdict, score, prose_lead, why_go, why_not
) VALUES
('siddhatek', 1, 'go', 4, 'January at Siddhatek runs at clean post-festival operational tempo. Siddhivinayak (the accomplishment-granting form of Ganesha — sought by saint Vishnu before his battle with the demons Madhu and Kaitabh) sits on a small Bhima river island in Karjat tehsil of Ahmednagar district, 100km from Pune via the Daund route. This is the only Ashtavinayak with a right-trunk murti (siddhi direction, opposite to the standard left-trunk Ganesh form) — pilgrims who specifically time their yatra to include the right-trunk darshan come here as the unique stop. The 1810 reconstruction by Punyashlok Ahilyabai Holkar — the Maratha Malwa queen who restored Hindu temples across northern India — defines the present structure. Daytime 14-29C, nights 8-10C. The Bhima river at clean post-monsoon flow; the small fishing-boat crossing from Shidoli (the road-end ghat on the Pune-facing river bank) runs ₹30-50 per pilgrim, 5-minute crossing. Sankashti Chaturthi early month brings Tuesday density. Combine optionally with Bhigwan Bird Sanctuary 30km west for an extension stop.', 'January 14-29C clean weather. Right-trunk Siddhivinayak (only one of 8) on Bhima river island. 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar reconstruction. Boat from Shidoli ₹30-50, 5 min crossing. Combine with Bhigwan Bird Sanctuary 30km.', NULL),
('siddhatek', 2, 'go', 5, 'February makes Siddhatek a Maghi Ganesh Jayanti centerpiece. The festival — Magh Shukla Chaturthi — falls Wednesday 4 February 2026; as the only right-trunk Ashtavinayak (siddhi direction — distinctive among the eight temples), Siddhatek attracts dedicated yatra-pilgrims who specifically time their visit for this configuration alongside the festival. The Siddhivinayak murti receives the pre-dawn maha-abhishek at 4am; palki processions run morning and evening. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 3 February 2026 compounding pilgrim density. Daytime 16-30C — clean temple weather. The Bhima river at clean low flow; the small fishing-boat crossing from Shidoli operating at reliable schedule. The 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar reconstruction (visible in the temple sanctum stonework and the surrounding wall) at full ritual tempo. The 100km Pune drive via Daund takes 2.5 hours on festival days. The remote location keeps Siddhatek less crowded than the Pune-cluster Ashtavinayak temples. Lodgings at Daund or Patas (15km) ₹600-1,800 festival rates.', 'Maghi Ganesh Jayanti Feb 4 + Angarki Feb 3 at only right-trunk Ashtavinayak. Pre-dawn maha-abhishek. 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar reconstruction. Bhima river crossing reliable. Daund lodgings ₹600-1,800. Less crowded than Pune-cluster.', NULL),
('siddhatek', 3, 'go', 4, 'March at Siddhatek holds clean operational temperature through the first three weeks. Gudi Padwa Thursday 19 March 2026 brings extended morning ritual at Siddhivinayak with Marathi New Year pilgrim flow building from Pune and Daund area. Daytime 21-34C, nights 14-16C — the Bhima river island setting (the small island sits surrounded by the river current on three sides, with the temple structure in the center and short pilgrim path encircling it) holds slightly cooler than the surrounding Daund plateau. The Siddhivinayak right-trunk murti and the 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar structure at full ritual tempo. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month standard density. The 100km Pune drive via Daund remains 2.5 hours; the Shidoli-side fishing-boat crossing reliable. Combine with Bhigwan Bird Sanctuary 30km west on the return leg. By final week the heat ramp arrives — Daund-plateau temperatures climb sharply. Lodgings at Daund ₹500-1,400. Last clean-comfort window before April compression.', 'Gudi Padwa Mar 19 extended ritual at Siddhivinayak right-trunk murti. 21-34C first 3 weeks. Bhima island setting slightly cooler than Daund plateau. Combine with Bhigwan Bird Sanctuary 30km. Last clean window before April.', NULL),
('siddhatek', 4, 'wait', 3, 'April pushes Siddhatek into heat-compromise territory. Daytime 27-40C on the Daund plateau — Bhima river island provides 2-3C of natural cool but the heat remains significant. The Siddhivinayak darshan compresses to pre-9am and post-5pm windows. The 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar stone interior holds cooler 33-35C through the day. The right-trunk murti (the distinctive feature of this Ashtavinayak) sits in the cool sanctum but the open pradakshina pilgrim path around the small island is exposed. The Bhima river at lowest pre-monsoon flow — the boat crossing from Shidoli operates on a near-walking-depth river that exposes its rocky bed by April-end. Pilgrim arrivals thin sharply through month; lodging rates at Daund drop to ₹400-1,000. The 100km Pune drive via Daund remains drivable but the temple visit collapses to dawn-only operations. The remote location combined with the heat makes Siddhatek the most-skipped Ashtavinayak through April. Push to October.', 'April compresses Siddhivinayak darshan to dawn and dusk. 27-40C Daund plateau, island provides 2-3C natural cool. Right-trunk murti accessible but pradakshina path exposed. Bhima at lowest flow. Push to October.', 'April runs at fragmented schedule. Heat compresses right-trunk Siddhivinayak darshan to dawn fragments. Remote Daund-plateau location combined with 27-40C makes Siddhatek the most-skipped Ashtavinayak through April.'),
('siddhatek', 5, 'skip', 2, 'May is unviable Siddhatek. Daytime 31-43C on the Daund plateau — among the hottest stretches in central Maharashtra; the temple stone island hits 50C surface noon. The right-trunk Siddhivinayak darshan continues but the practical pilgrim experience collapses — even the 5am dawn slot opens at 28C and reaches 36C by closing. The 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar stone interior holds 33-35C through the day. The Bhima river at year-low flow — the boat crossing from Shidoli operates on knee-deep water that exposes the rocky bed. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 5 May 2026 — dedicated pilgrim flow continues at modest density but most committed yatra-pilgrims skip Siddhatek through May. Lodgings at Daund drop to ₹400-900 deep off-season. The 100km Pune drive via Daund remains drivable but the temple visit collapses. The remote location with limited shade and minimal AC accommodation at Daund makes Siddhatek the deepest off-season Ashtavinayak in May. Push to October.', NULL, 'May 31-43C — Daund plateau year-hottest stretch. Temple island 50C surface noon. Even 5am dawn slot opens at 28C and reaches 36C. Bhima at year-low flow on knee-deep crossing. Remote location with limited shade and minimal AC accommodation at Daund. Push to October.'),
('siddhatek', 6, 'wait', 3, 'June marks southwest monsoon arrival in Siddhatek. First-week rains break the heat — daytime 22-32C, nights 19-21C. The Bhima river starts to swell visibly through the month; the small fishing-boat crossing from Shidoli runs more cautiously as the current strengthens by mid-month. The Siddhivinayak right-trunk darshan continues at standard schedule — the temple structure on the island remains dry as the river runs around the elevated platform. The 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar structure handles the monsoon arrival without strain. The Daund-plateau monsoon setting around the island temple is photographically striking. By final week the boat crossing becomes weather-dependent on heavy-rain days — the river current makes the small fishing-boats unsafe on flood-warning days. The 100km Pune drive via Daund takes 2.5-3 hours through monsoon delays. Sankashti Chaturthi late month brings modest pilgrim flow. Lodgings at Daund ₹500-1,300 with monsoon discount.', 'June monsoon arrival — 22-32C, fresh Daund-plateau context around Bhima island temple. 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar structure handles arrival. Boat crossing becomes weather-dependent by final week — river current strengthens.', 'June transition month — Bhima river swells, boat crossing weather-dependent by final week, heavy-rain days unsafe. 100km Pune-Daund drive 2.5-3 hours through delays. Operating window narrows as monsoon establishes.'),
('siddhatek', 7, 'skip', 2, 'July is unsafe Siddhatek. Bhima river at peak monsoon flow — the boat crossing from Shidoli suspends regularly through the month on flood-warning days. The temple foot-bridge (used in dry season as an alternate to the boat) submerges fully through July. The small fishing-boats cannot operate against the strong river current on heavy-rain days. The Siddhivinayak right-trunk darshan continues at the island temple — the 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar structure remains dry on its elevated platform — but pilgrim access becomes unreliable. ASI and the local temple trust post weekly access advisories; on flood-warning weeks the temple operates with priest-only puja and no pilgrim darshan. The Daund-plateau monsoon-soaked landscape around the island is photographically striking but operationally compromised. The 100km Pune drive via Daund takes 3-3.5 hours through caution sections. Sankashti Chaturthi pilgrim flow minimal. MTDC and MSRTC yatra packages drop Siddhatek from July itineraries. Push to October.', NULL, 'July Bhima river at peak monsoon flow — boat crossing suspends regularly on flood-warning days. Temple foot-bridge submerges fully. Pilgrim darshan unreliable. MTDC/MSRTC yatra packages drop Siddhatek from July itineraries. Push to October post-monsoon window.'),
('siddhatek', 8, 'skip', 2, 'August holds monsoon-peak conditions at Siddhatek — Bhima river remains at high flow and the boat crossing continues to suspend on flood-warning days. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 4 August 2026 — committed yatra-pilgrims attempt the crossing on weather-dry days; the Siddhatek temple trust schedules a special boat fleet for the Angarki day but operations remain weather-dependent. The Siddhivinayak right-trunk darshan continues at the island temple but pilgrim access remains unreliable through the bulk of August. The 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar structure remains dry on its elevated platform. Daytime 22-30C, humid; rainfall sustained at 300-450mm. The 100km Pune drive via Daund takes 2.5-3 hours through caution sections. Pre-Ganesh-Chaturthi build through final week brings dedicated pilgrim flow but most yatra packages continue to skip Siddhatek through August. Lodgings at Daund ₹500-1,200. Push to September festival window or October post-monsoon.', NULL, 'August Bhima river remains at high flow — boat crossing continues weather-dependent. Angarki Aug 4 pilgrims attempt risk but operations unreliable. Most yatra packages continue to skip Siddhatek through August. Push to September Ganesh Chaturthi or October.'),
('siddhatek', 9, 'go', 5, 'September makes Siddhatek a Ganesh Chaturthi anchor — and the post-monsoon reopening of reliable Bhima river island access. The festival (Bhadrapada Shukla Chaturthi) falls Saturday 12 September 2026 — the 10-day festival running through Anant Chaturdashi Tuesday 22 September 2026. The Siddhivinayak right-trunk murti — the only such configuration among the eight Ashtavinayak — receives continuous palki processions, special pre-dawn maha-abhishek every morning, full puran-poli and ukadiche-modak prasad distribution. The 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar structure runs at festival saturation. The Bhima river drops to navigable monsoon-tail flow through the first two weeks; the boat crossing from Shidoli resumes reliable operations by mid-month. Daytime 22-30C with monsoon tail rains tapering through first week. The 100km Pune drive via Daund takes 3-3.5 hours through festival traffic. Lodgings at Daund book 90 days ahead at ₹1,500-3,500 festival rates. Yatra package operators reinstate Siddhatek in their itineraries for September.', 'Ganesh Chaturthi Sep 12-22 — right-trunk Siddhivinayak (only one of 8) at festival saturation. Boat crossing reopens reliably mid-month. 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar structure. Daund lodgings ₹1,500-3,500. Yatra packages reinstate.', NULL),
('siddhatek', 10, 'go', 5, 'October is post-monsoon ideal Siddhatek. The 10-day Ganesh Chaturthi peak has dispersed; through the first two weeks the residue continues at strong tempo, then settles into clean operational tempo. Daytime 19-32C, nights 16-18C. Bhima river at full post-monsoon flow; the boat crossing from Shidoli runs reliably with the river current strong but safe for the small fishing-boats. The Siddhivinayak right-trunk murti and the 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar structure sit in cleanest visual presentation. The Daund-plateau backdrop with monsoon-green cover at peak photographic clarity. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 6 October 2026 bringing dedicated pilgrim density without the September overload. The 100km Pune drive via Daund returns to 2.5-hour standard time. Lodgings at Daund drop to ₹700-1,800. Combine with Bhigwan Bird Sanctuary 30km west — October migration arrivals (flamingos, pelicans, ducks) begin building through the month.', 'Post-monsoon ideal — 19-32C, Bhima at full flow, boat crossing reliable. Right-trunk Siddhivinayak at cleanest visual. Angarki Tue Oct 6. Combine with Bhigwan Bird Sanctuary 30km — October flamingo/pelican migration starts.', NULL),
('siddhatek', 11, 'go', 5, 'November is the year-best Siddhatek. The post-monsoon Daund-plateau green holds through first two weeks; daytime 16-30C, nights 12-14C — the sharpest cool weather of the year. The right-trunk Siddhivinayak darshan at full schedule with light woolens needed for the 5am slot. The 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar stone structure on the Bhima island holds light winter morning hue distinctively. The Bhima river at clean post-monsoon flow; the boat crossing from Shidoli runs reliable at strong-but-safe current. The remote island temple setting at its most evocative — the early winter mist over the river morning fog, the right-trunk murti silhouetted against the dawn cool, the small island silhouette in the slow-moving Bhima. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month standard Tuesday density. The 100km Pune drive via Daund runs 2.5 hours. Lodgings at Daund ₹700-1,800. Combine with Bhigwan Bird Sanctuary 30km — peak migration arrivals.', 'November year-best — 16-30C, sharpest cool. Right-trunk Siddhivinayak + 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar Bhima island setting at cleanest. Early winter mist over the river. Combine with Bhigwan Bird Sanctuary 30km peak migration.', NULL),
('siddhatek', 12, 'go', 4, 'December at Siddhatek opens with Angarki Chaturthi — Tuesday 1 December 2026, the auspicious month-opener pulling dedicated pilgrim flow. The right-trunk Siddhivinayak runs full ritual schedule with strong first-week density. Daytime 14-29C, nights 9-11C — year-coolest stretch; light woolens essential for 5am dawn slot, shawls for the early-morning boat crossing from Shidoli. The 1810 Ahilyabai Holkar Bhima island structure at clean visual presentation against the cool dry plateau. The river at moderate flow; boat crossing reliable. The 100km Pune drive via Daund runs heavy weekend traffic through Pune-tourist-escape season — 15 percent longer through December weekends. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month standard flow. Combine with Bhigwan Bird Sanctuary 30km west — December is peak flamingo viewing month at Bhigwan. Lodgings at Daund rise to ₹800-2,000. Book mid-month weekdays.', 'Dec 1 Angarki Chaturthi opens strong. 14-29C year-coolest. Right-trunk Siddhivinayak + Bhima island setting cleanest. Combine with Bhigwan Bird Sanctuary 30km — peak flamingo viewing month. Daund lodgings ₹800-2,000.', NULL)
ON CONFLICT (destination_id, month) DO UPDATE SET
  verdict = EXCLUDED.verdict,
  score = EXCLUDED.score,
  prose_lead = EXCLUDED.prose_lead,
  why_go = EXCLUDED.why_go,
  why_not = EXCLUDED.why_not;
